    {
      "index": 1,
      "code": "// Coffee mug — replicad/BREP showcase: cylinder body with a cut cavity, a\n// torus-loop handle standing out from the wall, and coffee filling the cavity.\n// Colours (white ceramic, blue rim band, brown coffee) are applied as\n// coordinate paint regions on the baked entry, so the code stays pure geometry.\nconst { BREP } = api;\n\n// Body: 50 mm dia (r 25), 70 mm tall, floor on z=0, 2.5 mm walls, open top.\nconst body = BREP.cylinder(25, 70);\n\n// Handle: a torus (major 13, minor 3.5) stood up so its ring lies in the XZ\n// plane, centred 29 mm out and at mid-height. Its outer edge reaches x=45.5\n// (20 mm clear of the wall) around a 19 mm finger opening. The inner half of\n// the ring is buried in the wall and trimmed back by the cavity cut below,\n// so only the graspable loop shows.\nconst handle = BREP.torus(13, 3.5).rotate(90, [1, 0, 0]).translate([29, 0, 35]);\n\nconst solid = body.fuse(handle);\n\n// Cavity: r 22.5 from the 2.5 mm floor up through the open rim. Cutting after\n// the handle fuse keeps the handle out of the cavity.\nconst mug = solid.cut(BREP.cylinder(22.5, 70).translate([0, 0, 2.5]));\n\n// Coffee: fills the cavity from the floor up to z=55. Radius 23 bites 0.5 mm\n// into the inner wall and the base starts at z=2 (inside the floor), so the\n// coffee is fused to the mug — ONE solid, nothing floating.\nconst coffee = BREP.cylinder(23, 53).translate([0, 0, 2]);\n\nreturn mug.fuse(coffee);\n",
